---
/**
 * Our Story - DESIGN.md 14.2. Copy from COPY.md, "Our Story", verbatim.
 *
 * Section rhythm: shader masthead -> paper -> paper-warm -> paper -> paper ->
 * paper-cool. Two --paper sections run back to back (4 and 5); that is fine,
 * the rule only forbids two COLOURED grounds sitting adjacent.
 *
 * [HISTORY] (COPY.md, between the pull quote and section 3) is intentionally
 * not rendered. No founding year exists in any source, COPY.md says not to
 * invent one, and the page is written to read as complete without it.
 */
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import Masthead from '../components/Masthead.astro';
import Section from '../components/Section.astro';
import SectionHeader from '../components/SectionHeader.astro';
import Divider from '../components/Divider.astro';
import HairlineList from '../components/HairlineList.astro';
import HairlineRow from '../components/HairlineRow.astro';
import Media from '../components/Media.astro';
import Button from '../components/Button.astro';

import { labels } from '../data/site';

const moments = [
  {
    marker: 'THE MORNING',
    title: 'Arabic and Deen.',
    body: 'Arabic classes are grouped by a placement test, so a child sits with others reading at the same level. Deen classes are grouped by age, so a child sits with others asking the same questions.',
  },
  {
    marker: 'SALAT AL-DHUHR',
    title: 'The morning ends.',
    body: 'Class runs until the midday prayer. Then everyone goes home to the rest of their Sunday, with something to do together during the week.',
  },
];
---

<Base
  title="Our Story - Islamic School of Potomac"
  description="We were founded to uplift every member of the family, not only the students registered in our school. This is what that means on a Sunday morning."
>
  {/* 1. Masthead */}
  <Masthead preset="story" label="ABOUT THE SCHOOL" lines={['More than', 'a Sunday school.']} />

  {/* 2. The founding commitment */}
  <Section ground="paper" grid>
    <p class="t-lead founding__lead" data-motion="body-rise">
      Most Sunday schools are built around a student. This one was built around a family.
    </p>

    <div class="founding__col founding__col--1">
      <p class="t-body" data-motion="body-rise">
        The Islamic School of Potomac teaches children ages 5 through 18, September through May.
        Arabic, Deen, and a third part of the program the school has never quite been able to
        name, so it calls it "...and in between."
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="founding__col founding__col--2">
      <p class="t-body" data-motion="body-rise">
        What holds those three together is not a curriculum. It is the understanding that a child
        does not learn a way of living for two hours on a Sunday and then set it down. What the
        school teaches has to be carried home, and the person who carries it is a parent.
      </p>
    </div>

    <blockquote class="founding__quote">
      <p class="t-title t-italic" data-motion="line-rise">
        The Islamic School of Potomac was founded with a commitment to uplift every member of the
        family, not just the students registered in our school.
      </p>
    </blockquote>
  </Section>

  {/* 3. A community, not a school */}
  <Section ground="warm" container="none">
    <div class="community">
      {/* 4.5 - bleeds to the viewport edge on the LEFT only, mirroring the
          homepage "Standing behind the school" row, which bleeds right. */}
      <div class="community__media">
        <Media slotId="story.opening" sizes="(min-width: 1024px) 50vw, 100vw" />
      </div>

      <div class="community__col">
        <SectionHeader label="WHO IS HERE" headline="We are a community." class="community__header" />
        <div class="flow community__body">
          <p class="t-body" data-motion="body-rise">
            The families who send their children here are the same people who set out the chairs,
            teach the classes, run the Showcase and answer the email. That is not a shortage of
            staff dressed up as a virtue. It is how a school this size stays honest: nobody here is
            being paid to tell you it is going well.
          </p>
          <p class="t-body" data-motion="body-rise">
            It also means the school is exactly as good as the people who show up for it, which is
            the most persuasive thing we can say about it.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </Section>

  {/* 4. What a Sunday is */}
  <Section ground="paper" grid>
    <div class="morning__header">
      <SectionHeader
        label="THE MORNING"
        headline="One morning a week, for thirty-three weeks."
      />
    </div>

    <div class="morning__list">
      <Divider />
      <HairlineList>
        {
          moments.map((moment) => (
            <HairlineRow marker={moment.marker} title={moment.title}>
              <p class="t-body">{moment.body}</p>
            </HairlineRow>
          ))
        }
      </HairlineList>
    </div>
  </Section>

  {/* 5. Volunteers */}
  <Section ground="paper" grid>
    <div class="volunteers__text">
      <SectionHeader
        label="HOW IT RUNS"
        headline="Parent feedback and volunteering is encouraged."
      >
        <p class="t-body" data-motion="body-rise">
          That sentence has been on this school's FAQ page for years, and it is doing more work
          than it looks like. Volunteering is not a way to help out at the margins here. It is the
          mechanism. If you have an hour, a skill, or a strong opinion about how something should
          be run, the school would rather hear it than not.
        </p>
        <div class="volunteers__cta" data-motion="body-rise">
          <Button href="/contact" variant="quiet" icon="arrow-right">{labels.contact}</Button>
        </div>
      </SectionHeader>
    </div>

    {/*
      DESIGN.md 14.2 asks for a 4/5 photo here; the only story-page slot for
      this content (adults setting up a room) is story.volunteers, seeded at
      its own 5/4. Per FOUNDATION.md the ratio belongs to the slot - the same
      call ProgramBrief.astro makes on the homepage.
    */}
    <div class="volunteers__media">
      <Media slotId="story.volunteers" sizes="(min-width: 1024px) 28vw, 90vw" />
    </div>
  </Section>

  {/* 6. CTA */}
  <Section ground="cool">
    <div class="cta">
      <SectionHeader headline="Come and see a Sunday." />
      <p class="t-body" data-motion="body-rise">
        Enrollment for 2026-2027 is open. Tuition is $60 for one student and $100 for a family, and
        financial assistance is available to anyone who needs it.
      </p>
      <div class="cta__actions" data-motion="body-rise">
        <Button href="/enroll" variant="primary">{labels.enrollPrimary}</Button>
        <Button href="/program" variant="quiet" icon="arrow-right">{labels.program}</Button>
      </div>
    </div>
  </Section>
</Base>

<style>
  /* ---- 2. The founding commitment ---- */

  .founding__lead,
  .founding__col,
  .founding__quote {
    grid-column: 1 / -1;
  }

  .founding__quote {
    margin: 0;
    margin-block-start: var(--s-8);
    padding-block-start: var(--s-6);
    border-block-start: var(--border-thin) solid var(--rule-accent);
  }

  @media (min-width: 768px) {
    .founding__lead { grid-column: 1 / 9; }
    .founding__col--1 { grid-column: 1 / 6; }
    .founding__col--2 { grid-column: 6 / 11; }
    .founding__quote { grid-column: 1 / 11; }
  }

  @media (min-width: 1024px) {
    .founding__lead { grid-column: 2 / 9; }
    .founding__col--1 { grid-column: 2 / 7; }
    .founding__col--2 { grid-column: 6 / 11; }
    .founding__quote { grid-column: 2 / 11; }
  }

  /* ---- 3. A community, not a school ---- */

  .community {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: var(--s-7);
  }

  .community__col {
    padding-inline: var(--gutter);
  }

  :global(.community__header) {
    margin-block-end: var(--s-5);
  }

  .community__body {
    max-width: var(--measure);
  }

  @media (min-width: 1024px) {
    .community {
      display: grid;
      grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr) minmax(0, 1fr);
      align-items: center;
      gap: var(--grid-gap);
    }

    /* The left column (the photo) already reaches the viewport edge; the
       right column's inner edge aligns to the container's own gutter, same
       maths as the homepage support row, mirrored left-to-right. */
    .community__col {
      margin-inline: 0;
      margin-inline-end: max(var(--gutter), calc(50vw - var(--container) / 2));
      padding-inline: 0;
      max-width: calc(var(--container) / 2 - var(--gutter));
    }
  }

  /* ---- 4. What a Sunday is ---- */

  .morning__header,
  .morning__list {
    grid-column: 1 / -1;
  }

  .morning__list {
    margin-block-start: var(--s-7);
  }

  @media (min-width: 768px) {
    .morning__header { grid-column: 1 / 9; }
    .morning__list { grid-column: 1 / 10; }
  }

  @media (min-width: 1024px) {
    .morning__header { grid-column: 2 / 9; }
    .morning__list { grid-column: 2 / 10; }
  }

  /* ---- 5. Volunteers ---- */

  .volunteers__text,
  .volunteers__media {
    grid-column: 1 / -1;
  }

  .volunteers__cta {
    margin-block-start: var(--s-2);
  }

  @media (min-width: 768px) {
    .volunteers__text { grid-column: 1 / 6; }
    .volunteers__media { grid-column: 6 / 11; }
  }

  @media (min-width: 1024px) {
    .volunteers__text { grid-column: 1 / 5; }
    .volunteers__media {
      grid-column: 6 / 9;
      margin-block-start: var(--s-8);
    }
  }

  /* ---- 6. CTA ---- */

  .cta {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: var(--s-5);
    max-width: var(--measure);
  }

  .cta__actions {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: var(--s-5) var(--s-7);
    margin-block-start: var(--s-2);
  }
</style>
